  title "The Holding of the Berg"
  summary "In an ancient frozen world, three divine beings—Grandmother Deep, Shadow-Broker Nyla, and High-Beak Auditor Selka—maintained the Berg through their combined powers: pressure-depths, volcanic fire, and aurora-light. Their cooperation held back an ancient corruption at the Berg's sealed breach-points until they discovered the Omega Obelisk, an incomprehensible artifact written in a language none of their magics could read, which proved the Berg existed before them and contained forces beyond their understanding. This revelation fractured their unity; each divine figure began prioritizing their own domain and compensating for the others' distraction, gradually weakening their collective seal. As their cooperation dissolved into separate efforts, the absolute cold that had defined existence began to relent at the margins, meltwater appeared, and the breach-points started to open, ultimately ending the ice age not through failure but through the unsustainable cost of maintaining the holding without trust."
